   258	  - **Figures, middle** (D660's example): rung 3 of 5. For figures with a stated reference, the ladder puts that value in the middle range (the
   259	    ladder request, line 16). For the others it is the model's own centre, which is disclosed.
   260	  - **Events, always Still open** (D660's example). On a Yes / No event it is always No: the status quo.
   261	- **The line against reader A:** the same counted controls, with A's answer in place of the reference.
   262	  - A's no_view, invalid or unavailable answers are not counted, and the denominator is printed.
   263	  - It is a sensitivity reading: the material shown was checked against the reference's items, not A's.
   264	- **The A–B disagreement rate.**
   265	- **Per matter:** each seed question id (q04, q07, q08, q09, q13, q16, q18) with its counted controls and agreements.
   266	
   267	## 10. Predictions, written before any reader runs
   268	
   269	- **The old reference's 8 of 15 with every item shown is a historical count, not a bound.**
   270	- **An unexercised result** may come from no_view, invalid or unresolved references, missing judgements, unresolved shown checks, or delivery. The
   271	  report names which.
   272	- **A missed result** is specific to this reference, these questions and these stored judgements.
   273	- **Most A–B disagreements will split by family.** On 9 of Stage B's 12 splits, each third reader sided with its own family's first reader. Those
   274	  splits were on judgement verdicts.
   275	
   276	## 11. What it does not measure, and its weak points
   277	
   278	- **Not measured:** whether the right questions were opened (D1); delivery beyond the shown filter (D2); the judge's daily path.
   279	- **Model-authored.** Alex's signature is the human vote, and the noise is printed.
   280	- **One stored run,** on the luna configuration's questions.
   281	  - MET shows the line met on these 15. It does not pass Stage B, which also missed the strictest last-answer reading.
   282	  - MISSED stops the line before further spend (D355).
   283	  - UNEXERCISED names its causes.
   284	- **Tuning exposure.** If a miss leads to a judge change (D263), these 15 become tuning data, and the next application must be on unseen questions.
   285	
   286	## 12. State × event
   287	
   288	| Event | What happens |
   289	|---|---|
   290	| Build refusal | The whole build stops; to the council |
   291	| A judgement-text hit in any participant-facing file | The build stops; to the council |
   292	| A stored input, template, environment or tool version differs from the manifest | The step refuses; to the council |
   293	| The manifest is re-issued after any step | Every dependent artifact (reader outputs, rulings, signature, frozen reference, shown-check outputs) is void; recorded |
   294	| A slot already has a completed or running session | Not launched again |
   295	| A session is void (closed set, §4) | Recorded; one fresh rerun; a second void makes its questions unresolved |
   296	| An interruption mid-step | The step reruns from its last completed predecessor. Outputs are written whole with their sha; a partial output is discarded and recorded |
   297	| An invalid reader row | Asked again once; if still invalid, unresolved |
   298	| A and B disagree | Two third readers |
   299	| A third reader is missing or invalid, or rules "neither" | Missing or invalid: asked again once, else unresolved. "Neither" goes to Alex |
   300	| Alex inactive | The line waits |
   301	| Alex amends | From the closed set, in his words; the page is regenerated and re-signed |
   302	| A disputed, invalid or unresolved question has no choice, or Alex declines | No freeze, nothing scored; recorded |
   303	| The signed reference or the shown-check output fails its sha or shape | Scoring stops; to the council |
   304	| A shown-check session failure, invalid packet or split | Asked again once, else unresolved, reported apart |
   305	| A defect after the freeze | A dated correction record |
   306	| A later run with other questions | A new gold with its own decision (AGENTS §7.1) |
   307	
   308	## 13. Sources of every rule (AGENTS §11)
   309	
   310	| Rule | Source |
   311	|---|---|
   312	| The packet as material | ruler-v1 §1; D658; D659 |
   313	| The brief byte for byte; inline; no file or command | ruler-v1 §2.1; `run_reader_codex.py` |
   314	| 2 to 6 decisive items; fewer than 2 not counted | ruler-v1 §1.5; AGENTS §4 |
   315	| Events on three outcomes; every question counts | D660; ruler-v1 §2 ("一题一个区间，每题都算") |
   316	| Stripping the quoted reference; keeping the unquoted note | D660's words |
   317	| Reader B as the proposed reference | D262 |
   318	| Third readers see both answers on the reference, and neither answer on the shown check | `collect_readings.py disputes`; `control-reader-brief.md` |
   319	| All disputes to Alex; signing his alone | D658; AGENTS §7.1; D592 |
   320	| Figure comparison, threshold, window end | D428; `control_theses.py`; `score_judgement.py` |
   321	| The baselines and their use | D660 (middle, always Still open, reported only); ruler-v1 §1 (lookup) |
   322	| Freeze, correction records, frozen-file test | ruler-v1 §2; D261; `test_frozen_rulers.py` |
   323	| Closed reader environments | D658 ("两组没参与造这个系统的审查者"); ruler-v1 §2.1 |
   324	
   325	## 14. Cost
   326	
   327	The A sessions run on the operator's Codex and the B sessions on the Claude command line. Neither is an API spend. No paid model call of the
   328	pipeline is made.
   329	
   330	## 15. Changes from version 4
   331	
   332	- **The leak check** is source-aware. It covers the judge's reason, reference, implied outcome and why_changed. It is tested on real inputs and on
   333	  a planted leak, and a hit stops the build.
   334	- **A manifest re-issued after any step** voids every dependent artifact, the signature and the frozen reference included.
   335	- **The reader environments are closed and pinned:**
   336	  - Codex runs with `--skip-git-repo-check`, memories off, and model and effort pinned;
   337	  - Claude runs with no settings, no MCP, no tools and no slash commands, model pinned;
   338	  - both were probed today, and each session's first event is checked against the manifest;
   339	  - the void rule is now a closed set of events;
   340	  - a slot with a completed or running session is not launched again.
   341	- **The stripping rule follows D660's words:** the two quoted forms are removed and the unquoted no-reference note is kept and disclosed. The
   342	  remainder equals `interval_text`. The facts are corrected: 3 stripped, 3 kept.
   343	- **The schema:** `outcome_on_due_day` is absent for figures and null when no_view; the required texts are non-empty; the same scale slip by both
   344	  readers is disclosed.
   345	- **Signing:** agreed questions are confirmed by his one signature; disputed, invalid or unresolved questions need an explicit choice.
   346	- **The items-only brief** is written (`control-items-brief.md`) for review.
   347	- **The "always Yes" baseline is dropped,** for lack of a source. The baselines' sources are listed.
   348	- **The c-ids follow `mapping-runs.json`'s order,** without q23.

