**Version 5 is not ready:** the leak check still needs a precise definition of each participant’s permitted inputs, and the retry rule can prevent a required retry.

- **Source-aware leak check:** It now allows shared packet passages and evidence, has a planted-leak test, and stops on a hit. But the permitted-source list does not include all legitimate content later participants must see. Third readers receive A and B’s answers; Alex’s page includes those answers, rulings, and stripped text. Those are not in the listed permitted sources, so an innocent eight-word overlap with a stored judgment could stop the process. Define permitted inputs separately for each stage and test the check on generated reconciliation and signing pages as well as the initial prompt. An eight-word check remains a limited leak detector, so the closed fields and fixed generators still matter. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:96), [reconciliation and signing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:167).

- **Resumption and retries:** Version 5 says a slot with a completed session is never launched again, but an invalid row must be asked again once. A session can complete successfully while returning an invalid row. Define the retry as a separate recorded attempt or slot, and check for an existing running or completed **retry** before launching it. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:135), [invalid-row rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:164).

- **Items-only brief:** The substantive shown/not-shown rule and blind third-reader procedure match the earlier brief. Its example uses a numeric control ID (`3`), while version 5 assigns `c01`–`c15`; fix the output contract to use one identity consistently so answers can be checked and reconciled without ambiguity. [Items brief](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/control-items-brief.md:20), [population](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:62).

The other round-4 findings are addressed: manifest re-issue voids dependent artifacts; the schema specifies the event field and required text; the unquoted no-reference note is retained and disclosed; and Alex’s single signature confirms agreed questions while disputed or unresolved questions need individual choices. The environment probes and closed event checks improve isolation, but the design’s own note that user-level Claude instructions may still load means their contents must be checked, not merely hashed, before the environment is accepted. [Manifest and invalidation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:14), [environment](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:120), [signing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/stage-b-controls/NEW-REFERENCE-DESIGN-v5.md:197).

NOT READY: Define stage-specific permitted inputs for the leak check, distinguish retry attempts, and align the items-check control IDs.
